---
title: Pappardelle with lamb ragu
tags: [italian, lamb, braise, weekend]
cuisine: italian
source: Lamb Ragu Pasta Recipe by Hilton, https://www.hilton.com/en/travel/articles/pappardelle-with-lamb-ragu
---

== Ragu ==

Salt the @lamb shoulder{2%lb} at least ~{4%hours} ahead, or overnight.

Heat the oven to 375°F (190°C). Sear the lamb in @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a
#rondeau{}, seasoning it with @black pepper{1.6%g}. Lift it out.

In the same pan, add the @onion{70%g}(diced), @carrot{70%g}(diced),
@fennel{70%g}(diced) and @celery{70%g}(diced) with @salt{4.9%g} and a little
pepper. Sweat ~{5-8%minutes}, scraping up the browned bits.

Add the @garlic{3%cloves}(minced), @ground cumin{1 1/3%g} and
@fennel seed{0.5%g}(toasted). Cook ~{5-8%minutes} more.

Pour in the @white wine{57.5%g} and stir to lift the fond. Tie the
@rosemary{2%g}, a @bay leaf{1} and a few black peppercorns in a sachet and drop
it in. Add the @tomato sauce{1%cup} and @lamb stock{1%cup}(roasted) and bring
to a gentle simmer.

Stir in the @calabrian chili{2 1/3%g} and return the lamb. Lay a cartouche on
the surface, cover the pan with foil, and braise at 300°F (149°C)
~{3.5-4%hours}, until the lamb is tender.

== Pappardelle ==

Mix the @00 flour{85%g}, @egg yolks{55%g} and @water{3.25%g} in a
#stand mixer{} ~{12%minutes}. Knead by hand ~{3%minutes}, then rest at room
temperature ~{30%minutes}.

Roll the dough out to the thickness you like and cut wide ribbons by hand.
Boil in salted water ~{4-5%minutes}.

== To serve ==

Warm a portion of ragu with a splash of water, add the pappardelle, and loosen
with a ladle of stock if needed.

Grate @Pecorino Romano{} over the top. Adjust with salt and a pinch of sugar,
and add @?chili oil{}(Calabrian) for heat and the juice of @?lemon{1/2} for
brightness.

Finish with shaved pecorino, a drizzle of @olive oil{} and a few fennel fronds.
